<title>HUNGARY: Hungary clears Russia oil trade suspects.</title>
<headline>Hungary clears Russia oil trade suspects.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Parliament on Tuesday cleared persons and companies accused of violating the law in Hungarian oil deals with Russia, Hungarian Radio said.</p>
<p>Parliament approved the report of a committee investigating the case, which is called &quot;Oilgate&quot; in the Hungarian press.</p>
<p>The parliament said the investigation had not uncovered any breach of the law by persons and companies involved the case, and decided that efforts to sell Hungarian goods in Russia served Hungary's interests, the radio added.</p>
<p>Hungary, which buys most of its oil from Russia, posts huge deficits in bilateral trade and strives to balance its oil purchases with the sale of more Hungarian products to Russia.</p>
</text>
